&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Coursera + Udemy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Coursera and Udemy are now one company, bringing together two mission-driven brands to create the world’s most powerful platform for turning learning into progress. Together, we help more than 300 million learners and 12,000+ enterprise customers build the skills they need for a world being reshaped by AI. Read more about the combined company by visiting our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://blog.coursera.org/coursera-and-udemy-are-now-one-company-creating-the-worlds-most-comprehensive-skills-platform/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;blog&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why join us now?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AI is transforming how people learn, work, and grow, and the need for new skills has never been greater. Coursera brings trusted content and credentials from leading university and industry partners, while Udemy brings a dynamic skills marketplace and global network of real-world experts. By combining these strengths, we can connect more people and organizations to the skills they need, when they need them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shape what comes next&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By joining our team, you’ll have the opportunity to reshape how the world learns and applies skills—and help millions of people participate in the new economy. Bring your ideas, expertise, and perspective to meaningful work that can make a difference at global scale.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and develop 3-4 globally-based Deal Desk Analysts, staying actively engaged in deal-level decisions rather than operating purely at a policy level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide hands-on guidance on complex or non-standard deals - structuring options, pricing trade-offs, negotiation strategy - and coach analysts toward independent commercial judgment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the escalation point on complex deals before Finance/Legal sign-off.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pricing &amp;amp; Discount Strategy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own discount governance, setting guardrails that balance deal velocity, margin, and customer experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze discounting trends and exception rates to identify leakage and drive refinements to commercial policy; build discount tiers and approval thresholds with Finance and Pricing &amp;amp; Packaging.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Surface pricing insights from market and deal-level analysis - where pricing is winning, losing, or leaving revenue on the table - and deliver that perspective to senior leadership and the teams who own pricing strategy, directly informing GTM sales motions like packaging and seller enablement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build pricing and discount playbooks tailored to specific regions and verticals, partnering with field sales to surface market and industry-specific needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deal Structuring &amp;amp; Analysis&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own commercial judgment on complex, high-value, or non-standard deals - structuring terms, payment schedules, multi-year commitments, and custom packaging to close revenue while protecting margin.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Enterprise sellers to model scenarios and trade-offs (discount depth vs. term vs. payment terms) and recommend winning structures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze historical deal data to identify what structures win, where deals stall, and where exceptions cluster - turning insights into playbooks and leadership recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operational Excellence &amp;amp; Reporting&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own Deal Desk KPIs (cycle time, discount depth, deal velocity, exceptions) and report on commercial health to leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own commercial approval frameworks within Salesforce CPQ, continuously simplifying workflows and reducing friction in the sales process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain clear documentation of policy and precedent to keep decisions consistent and auditable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Partnership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build strong rapport with Sales, Finance, Legal, and Product stakeholders, becoming a trusted point of contact for pricing and discounting questions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Co-own the development and refinement of commercial policy in partnership with Sales, Finance, Legal, and Product - actively shaping the guardrails these functions operate under, not just providing input.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Deal Desk in strategic planning discussions related to pricing strategy, packaging, and go-to-market evolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the field with pricing and discounting guidance tailored to regional and vertical realities rather than one-size-fits-all policy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Basic Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years in Deal Desk, Revenue Operations, Commercial Operations, Sales Operations, Finance, or Pricing, with a strong focus on pricing analysis and deal structuring.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years managing a globally distributed team (2+ reports), staying actively engaged in deal-level work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience presenting pricing and discounting analysis to leadership and influencing decisions beyond your own team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong relationship-building skills as a trusted pricing/discounting resource.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience owning or co-owning discount governance and pricing frameworks in Salesforce CPQ or a comparable quote-to-cash system.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to structure complex enterprise deals in a SaaS/subscription business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills turning deal data into actionable recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing or shaping commercial policy in partnership with cross-functional stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in high-growth B2B SaaS with a global or multi-region sales org.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing or coordinating across time zones with a global team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort as a player-coach who stays hands-on with deal guidance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience representing a function in broader strategic planning around pricing, packaging, or GTM evolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience tailoring pricing/discounting guidance to specific regions or verticals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with ASC 606 as it relates to deal structuring.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced Excel/Google Sheets modeling and executive presentation experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This role is available in the following US Pay Zones:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;US Zone 3: $158,950 - $187,000&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;US Zone 4: $148,325 - $174,500&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Coursera, we offer competitive, zone-based pay aligned to your location, experience, and role level across four U.S. pay zones. Our total rewards package goes beyond salary, with comprehensive health and wellness benefits, bonus and RSU equity programs, and global perks designed to help you grow and thrive wherever you are.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;US Pay Zones&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;US-Z1: Bay Area&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;US-Z2: NYC and Seattle Metro&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;US-Z3: CA, WA, NY, NJ, CO, CT, DC, GA, IL, MA, MD, OR, RI, TX, VA&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;US-Z4: AK, AZ, DE, FL, HI, ID, IN, IA, KS, KY, MI, MN, MO, MT, NC, NV, NH, OH, OK, PA, SC, TN, UT, VT, WI&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Posting Date: &lt;/strong&gt;8/29/2026&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Application Window:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We anticipate the application window will be open until 9/18/2026. Based on business needs, this opportunity may remain posted beyond or closed before the anticipated application window.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h6&gt;#LI-JC2&lt;/h6&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;For more information about how Coursera collects and uses your personal information, please see our &lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://files.clinchtalent.com/1d7f2c0f91ebf75d580f56447fa54859/2acb24eb91f1e23b90ac9e9285de5aaf/Coursera%20and%20Udemy%20Global%20Applicant%20Privacy%20Notice.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Coursera + Udemy Global Applicant Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;u&gt;.&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To protect against recruitment fraud, Coursera + Udemy recruiters only communicate via official coursera.org/udemy.com email addresses and never through personal accounts. We do not accept resumes via email or social media; please submit all applications directly through our careers page.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you encounter suspicious recruitment activity, please report it via our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://forms.gle/Mb8UktwuaJAukb3H7&quot;&gt;Fraudulent Activity Submission Form.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Coursera is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to building a welcoming and inclusive workplace. We consider all qualified applicants without regard to legally protected characteristics and provide reasonable accommodations upon request at recruiting@coursera.org.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
